  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Key Components",
      "items": [
        "A single VirtualService defines the routing rules for all zones",
        "A per-zone Rollout manages each zone's canary deployment independently",
        "Each Rollout touches only its own subset pair (stable-a/canary-a, etc.)",
        "The locality-aware DestinationRule handles zone-local routing and failover automatically"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Why This Avoids Conflicts",
      "items": [
        "Argo Rollouts overwrites the entire destinations array of the named route",
        "So each Rollout references a different route name: zone-a-route, zone-b-route, zone-c-route"
      ]
    }
  ]
